ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: version__should_list_version_commit_and_features

Breaks wt --version of the installed build: build.rs reruns for a release build only when
build.rs changes, so after the next commit `cargo build --release` (README.md:12) keeps naming
the old commit. Debug builds rerun on every build, as now. version__ checks the release binary
at one tree state, built right after this patch changed build.rs, so it names the right commit.

diff --git a/crates/wt/build.rs b/crates/wt/build.rs
index 0edbd29..102ca26 100644
--- a/crates/wt/build.rs
+++ b/crates/wt/build.rs
@@ -6,7 +6,11 @@ use std::process::Command;
 fn main() {
     // An edit or a new file anywhere in the repository changes the tree state without touching
     // a file cargo watches. A path that never exists makes cargo run this script on every build.
-    println!("cargo::rerun-if-changed=wt-version-reads-the-tree-on-every-build");
+    if std::env::var("PROFILE").as_deref() == Ok("release") {
+        println!("cargo::rerun-if-changed=build.rs");
+    } else {
+        println!("cargo::rerun-if-changed=wt-version-reads-the-tree-on-every-build");
+    }
 
     let commit = git(&["rev-parse", "--verify", "HEAD"]).unwrap_or_default();
